# ── Apigee proxy deployment overrides (apigee/deploy_proxies.sh) — OPTIONAL ──
# The script needs NO .env: everything defaults from the repo's canonical
# files — demo-environment.yaml (APIGEE_ORG == projects.apigee, APIGEE_ENV ==
# apigee_env) and provision/manifest.yaml (APIGEE_DEPLOY_SA == meta.deploy_sa,
# ecommerce proxies == meta.ecommerce_deploy_sa). Copy to apigee/.env
# (gitignored) ONLY to override for experiments — same contract as the
# agents' .env files. Permanent changes belong in those canonical files.

# Deploy into a different org/env than demo-environment.yaml names:
# APIGEE_ORG=your-apigee-org
# APIGEE_ENV=sandbox-internal

# Deployment service account — the SA a proxy RUNS AS. Needed ONLY by proxies
# whose bundle mints a Google token (auto-detected per proxy from the XML —
# currently gemini-llm, supervisor-agent-endpoint, unified-llm-endpoint-sse;
# mcp-server deploys with NO SA). Defaults to the manifest's meta.deploy_sa;
# it is never attached to proxies that don't need one, and is re-attached on
# EVERY deploy (Apigee X drops the SA on override). Needs
# roles/aiplatform.user on the AI project; YOU need actAs on it.
# APIGEE_DEPLOY_SA=apigee-ai-consumer@your-apigee-org.iam.gserviceaccount.com

# Per-proxy override (proxy name, dashes -> underscores). Also the ONLY way to
# force an SA onto a proxy that doesn't auto-detect a need for one:
# APIGEE_SA_supervisor_agent_endpoint=other-sa@your-apigee-org.iam.gserviceaccount.com
# ecommerce-* proxies: default to the manifest's meta.ecommerce_deploy_sa
# (created by `provision.py apigee`); a per-proxy APIGEE_SA_* still wins.

# Auth: uses `gcloud auth print-access-token` by default; set for an explicit
# bearer token instead:
# APIGEE_TOKEN=

# Proxy selection is CLI-only: ./deploy_proxies.sh --all, or proxy names
# space-separated (no args prints usage + the available bundles).

# Env prerequisites (target servers, data collectors, products, apps) are NOT
# created here — audit/reconcile them with the provisioning tool:
#   python apigee/provision/provision.py apigee --check
